findings.body:
The `testDownloadingSVGImage_withKingfisherProcessor_forStandardSVGCase` test now calls `downloadImage` and returns immediately. Its assertions are inside a Kingfisher completion handler that runs asynchronously. Because the `expectation` and `wait(for:)` were removed, XCTest can finish the test before those assertions run. A regression in SVG rendering would go undetected, and assertions that fire after a test ends can be reported against the wrong test or dropped.

The other SVG tests in this file still use `exp.fulfill()` and `wait(for: [exp], timeout: 2.0)`. This one should do the same.

::diff{file="BrowserKit/Tests/SiteImageViewTests/SVGImageProcessorTests.swift" lines="26-37"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The removed lines were not dead code. They were the only thing keeping this test waiting for the callback. Restore the expectation and wait, the same way the SVG case 2 test does.

::suggestion{file="BrowserKit/Tests/SiteImageViewTests/SVGImageProcessorTests.swift" lines="26-36"}
let exp = expectation(description: "Image download and parse")

let siteDownloader = DefaultSiteImageDownloader()
siteDownloader.downloadImage(with: mockedURL, options: [.processor(SVGImageProcessor())]) { result in
    switch result {
    case .success(let result):
        XCTAssertEqual(result.originalData, imageData)
        XCTAssertEqual(result.url, mockedURL)
        XCTAssertEqual(result.image.size, expectedRasterSize)
        exp.fulfill()
    case .failure(let error):
        XCTFail("Should not have an error: \(error) \(error.errorDescription ?? "")")
        exp.fulfill()
    }
}
wait(for: [exp], timeout: 2.0)

`startMockImageServer` used to carry `@MainActor` with a comment saying GCDWebServer must be initialized for the first time on the main thread, and that the annotation prevents a crash when this test file runs alone. Both the annotation and the comment were removed, and the tests now call the helper from non-isolated synchronous methods.

XCTest usually runs test methods on the main thread, so this may not crash today. But the invariant the comment documented is now gone, and nothing replaces it. If the tests are ever run in a different context, or the test class is moved to a background executor, the first `GCDWebServer()` initialization can happen off the main thread and fail intermittently.

::diff{file="BrowserKit/Tests/SiteImageViewTests/SVGImageProcessorTests.swift" lines="206-214"}

::callout{type="info"}
If the goal was to avoid `await` in these tests, keep the guard and make the helper `@MainActor` and call it from a `@MainActor` test or via `MainActor.assumeIsolated`. Otherwise, restore the comment and say why the guard is no longer needed.

The three-line Mozilla Public License header at the top of this file was deleted. The rest of BrowserKit carries this header, for example `SVGImageProcessorTests.swift` and `WKUIHandlerTests.swift`. The change is unrelated to the Swift 6 migration, and it breaks the repository's convention. Mozilla projects commonly run automated license-header checks, so this may also fail CI.

