The title and description say ShareTo was migrated to Swift 6. The only ShareTo change in the diff is `SWIFT_VERSION = 6.0` on six build configurations. The ShareTo sources are not touched, so any Swift 6 concurrency errors in them (for example around `NSItemProvider` callbacks or non-Sendable captures) would only appear when the target is compiled under Swift 6. The description says "No warnings as far as I can tell... let's see what Bitrise says", so this has not been compiled yet.

